--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What this covers, and what it does not

The MIT terms above cover the Lumos toolchain itself: the `lumos` CLI, its git
and assistant hooks, the installer scripts, the skills, and the documentation in
this repository.

They do not cover what the tool writes into your project. The discipline block
merged into your CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md, the graph notes you author, and every
other file the tool helps you produce are yours. Lumos claims nothing in them.

Note on vendored copies: `lumos init` / `update` / `bootstrap` copy a handful of
this repository's files into your project (the CLI, its hooks, a few helper
scripts). Each of those files carries an SPDX header, and the CLI itself carries
the full licence text in its header, so a copy stays self-describing even when
it travels alone. This LICENSE file is deliberately NOT copied into your project
— your project's own LICENSE is yours and the toolchain must never overwrite or
delete it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Third-party components

Bundled under `scripts/vendor/` and, when `lumos export --standalone` is used,
embedded verbatim into the generated HTML:

  marked 12.0.2 — MIT License
    Copyright (c) 2011-2024, Christopher Jeffrey (https://github.com/chjj/)
    https://github.com/markedjs/marked
    (Its own licence header is preserved verbatim at the top of the bundled file.)

  3d-force-graph 1.80.0 — MIT License
    Copyright (c) Vasco Asturiano
    https://github.com/vasturiano/3d-force-graph
    The upstream minified build ships without a licence banner, so the notice is
    reproduced here and in the generated HTML instead. Its bundle includes, all
    under permissive terms:
      three (r183) — MIT, Copyright (c) 2010-2025 three.js authors
      three-forcegraph, three-render-objects, kapsule, accessor-fn — MIT,
        Copyright (c) Vasco Asturiano
      d3-force-3d — MIT, Copyright (c) 2010-2024 Mike Bostock, Vasco Asturiano
      d3-binarytree, d3-dispatch, d3-octree, d3-quadtree, d3-timer — ISC,
        Copyright (c) 2010-2021 Mike Bostock
    This inner list is derived from the package's dependency tree, not from
    reading the minified bundle. Re-verify it if the pinned version changes.
